 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against the registered `inputSchema` before
+  calling the executor. A call with missing required properties or a wrong-typed field returns a
+  `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing constraint so the model can read it and retry —
+  the executor is never invoked for invalid input. Unknown extra properties pass through unchanged.
+  An invalid schema supplied at `register` time throws immediately so a misconfigured tool fails at
+  startup rather than mid-conversation.
+
