+# HAL Engine Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates a tool call against the registered tool's
+`inputSchema` before invoking its executor. A rejected input is returned as a
+`ToolResponse` whose result describes the validation failure, and the executor
+is not invoked.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects input missing a required property before the executor runs, returning a result that identifies that property as required ([validated by: rejects missing required tool input before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L31), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L12)).
+- The executor is not invoked when required tool input is missing ([validated by: does not invoke the executor when required tool input is missing](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- Valid input with extra unlisted properties is passed to the executor unchanged; the registry does not strip or coerce fields ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties to the executor unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L30)).
+- A validation error for a wrong-typed field names the field path and expected type, and never includes the field's value ([validated by: rejects wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L44)).
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` throws `Error('Unknown tool: <name>')` when the named tool is not registered ([validated by: throws for an unknown tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L54)).
